    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Catalan counties united under the counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, who were also kings of Aragon from 1162.</li><li>Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catalan-courts">Corts</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/generalitat-de-catalunya">Generalitat</a> and merchant capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> made it one of the most commercial and parliamentary states of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>Revolts in 1640 and 1705 ended in defeat, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nueva-planta-decrees">Nueva Planta</a> decree of 1716 abolished its institutions.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taula-de-canvi">Taula de Canvi</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>’s city council in 1401, was one of the first public banks in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, holding deposits and handling the city’s finances.</p></aside>
    </section>

